# The forced-command scripts run on the Linux servers. A CRLF working copy on Windows would
# break the shebang ("bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M") when copied across, so pin them
# to LF regardless of core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
# Read line by line by ip-allowlist.sh, which refuses a line ending in a CR as not an address.
*.extra text eol=lf

# systemd units are copied to the servers the same way and read the same way; a CR at the
# end of an ExecStart path is part of the path as far as systemd is concerned.
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer text eol=lf

# Brand assets: no line-ending conversion.
*.png binary
*.ico binary

# The decision log is append-only: every entry is a new line at the end of the file, so two
# branches that both record a decision conflict on that last line every time — three times in
# one session before this. Union merge keeps both sides instead, which is all an append-only
# log ever wanted. It keeps both sides of a rewritten line too, silently, so revising an
# existing entry is a merge to read rather than one to trust.
DECISIONS.md merge=union
